{"input_sha256":"db5fd146e074d55a5cbde338c3c35e75cbbe00c5d4d34feff738425d47c316f8","problem_sha256":"f76b3e036f1d63cc9d36ff3f18f497d6365f26dfb3faad836c262ab391ed8754","read_receipts":[{"object_id":"obj_2808dc0cd802e9efefc9f3bf9c149628f420df618eeea1e512c0efda43b0aa94","sha256":"86c4f134dcfa3d1ddf9df7da59efa1c04b5a26cc054a00d786d0ce88f7f18a5a","media_type":"application/json","size_bytes":7651}],"usage":{"provider_requests":null,"total_tokens":null},"output":{"briefing":"Work only on the exact universal claim and quantifiers in problem_contract. This direction has no recorded attempts, attempt feedback, review findings, dependency graph, or reusable lemmas; the goal remains open. The supplied artifact contains a candidate proof for the exact six-coordinate claim, but it is not an accepted proof. Its main route appears mathematically coherent on the supplied text: parity valuations for a,b; the size bound 0<|c|<8/9; an H-divisibility contradiction for e; and, for f,g, a prime p>3 dividing Q, noncancellation modulo p, and an order-eight element in F_p*. Verify the details independently rather than treating the candidate as established.

For a,b, check both parity cases, including that m²−7n² and 7m²−n² are nonzero (a zero would make 7 or 1/7 a rational square). When m,n are odd, verify v₂(H)=1, v₂(D)≥3, and valuation 1 for each of those two factors. For c, H±D=2m²,2n² establish 0<|D|<H. For e, integrality forces H to divide its numerator; modulo H that numerator is 32n⁴. Use gcd(H,n)=1, the fact that H has 2-adic valuation 0 or 1, and H≥5 to rule out H|32.

For the remaining claims, establish Q>0, the stated bounds v₂(Q)∈{0,2} and v₃(Q)∈{0,2}, and Q≥153; these imply Q has a prime divisor p>3. For any such p, show p∤mn,D,H. The candidate uses four polynomial identities to prove that the four numerator factors of f do not vanish at T=m/n modulo p; check each identity by multiplication or provide another explicit certificate. Then verify the numerator is a p-adic unit, giving vₚ(f)=−2vₚ(Q). Check the substitution g(m,n)=f(−m,n) and apply the same argument to g. Finally, from Q=D²+36m²n² and Q=H²+32m²n², the proposed r=D/(6mn) and s=H/(4mn) satisfy r²=−1 and s²=−2 in Fₚ. Verify that z=(s/r)(1+r)/2 satisfies z²=r and z⁴=−1; its order is then 8, forcing p≡1 mod 8. A constructive route may seek fresh explicit modular noncancellation certificates, such as computed gcd/resultant identities, but this is advisory: choose a method that proves the exact statements and checks all identities. Finite coefficient checks do not constitute formal proof-assistant verification. Do not extend the conclusion beyond the displayed rational family; the broader unrestricted-sign or all-positive sextuple existence question remains unresolved.","artifact_reading_list":["obj_2808dc0cd802e9efefc9f3bf9c149628f420df618eeea1e512c0efda43b0aa94"],"diversity_constraints":{"avoid_methods":[],"preferred_method_family":"constructive","must_differ_from_prior_attempts":true},"problem_contract":{"acceptance_profile":"reviewed","assumptions":["m,n are coprime integers with n>0, mn≠0, and m²≠n²; these are the reduced-parameter conditions for rational t outside {0,1,−1}.","H=m²+n², D=m²−n², Q=m⁴+34m²n²+n⁴, and the six rational coordinates are exactly the formulas stated in the lemma statement."],"objective":"proof","quantifiers":["For every pair of integers m,n satisfying the assumptions, with no height bound.","For every prime p>3 dividing the corresponding positive integer Q."],"source_refs":[],"statement":"For coprime integers m,n with n>0, mn≠0, and m²≠n², put H=m²+n², D=m²−n², and Q=m⁴+34m²n²+n⁴. Define a=−9H/(8D), b=(m²−7n²)H(7m²−n²)/(8D³), c=8D³/(9H³), e=−2(m²+5n²)(5m²+n²)/(9DH), f=−2mn(m²−4mn−3n²)(3m²−4mn−n²)(m³+8m²n+5mn²+4n³)(4m³−5m²n+8mn²−n³)/(DHQ²), and g=2mn(m²+4mn−3n²)(3m²+4mn−n²)(m³−8m²n+5mn²−4n³)(4m³+5m²n+8mn²+n³)/(DHQ²). Then none of a,b,c,e,f,g is an integer. Moreover, Q has a prime divisor p>3; every prime p>3 dividing Q satisfies p≡1 (mod 8) and vₚ(f)=vₚ(g)=−2vₚ(Q)."},"selected_lemma_ids":[],"uncertainties":["The supplied candidate proof is not recorded as accepted, and this snapshot has no attempt records or review findings; the next proof must substantiate the claims independently.","No formal proof-assistant verification or external literature search was performed. The checked source is only the supplied JSON artifact.","The object referenced by a nested historical receipt, obj_41923f60389eb9cfe812ae7cf74bc64d6a09027a5ec2002f752a4bfa86b169ed, was not supplied in this snapshot; its contents and any citations remain unchecked.","The broader unrestricted-sign or all-positive sextuple existence question is not resolved by this claim."]}}
